    "source_text": "The aim of the reaction is optimization.  Tris(dibenzylideneacetone)dipalladium(0) (4.5 mg, 4.91 µmol) and 9,9-Dimethyl-4,5-bis(diphenylphosphino)xanthene (5.1 mg, 8.81 µmol) were dissolved in dioxane (1.8 mL) in a 10 mL Schlenk tube and activated at 100 °C for 6 min under argon. Then 5-fluoro-4-(2-methyl-1-(tetrahydro-2H-pyran-4-yl)-1H-imidazol-5-yl)pyrimidin-2-amine (51 mg, 0.18 mmol), 4-(4-bromobenzyl)morpholine (51 mg, 0.20 mmol) and Cesium carbonate (94 mg, 0.29 mmol) were added. It was degassed again and stirred at 100 °C under argon.  The reaction was followed by HPLC. After 26 h 85.5 % conversion was obtained. 20 % by-product formation was detected.  Finally, the reaction mixture was discarded.  ",
    "text_sha256": "5f7eed5df7ce8daf65c1492dc13ae83adbecebc153c13ec88404c8bdf0f3627a",
